    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Director--Prospect-Management-and-Research_R0003534": {
      "title": "Director, Prospect Management and Research",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Director, Prospect Management and Research LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Advancement Operations DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Director of Prospect Management and Research provides strategic leadership and hands-on direction for WPI's prospect development program, encompassing prospect research, prospect management, and pipeline development. This position designs and implements the research standards, screening strategies, capacity rating methodologies, and portfolio management practices that identify and advance the University's major, principal, and planned gift prospects, directly supporting a successful fundraising pipeline and the University's advancement goals. Reporting to the Executive Director, Advancement Operations, the Director leads the prospect research team and serves as a trusted partner and consultant to gift officers and fundraising leadership, conducting prospect research, managing gift officer portfolios, and translating research insight and pipeline analysis into actionable prospect strategy. The Director collaborates closely with the Analytics, Gift Management, and Advancement Systems functions to ensure prospect information is accurate, well-governed, and effectively used across the division. JOB DESCRIPTION Prospect Development Strategy & Program Management Develop and implement processes that advance prospect management and research at WPI, including moves management, prospect pipeline development, portfolio development, prospect engagement measurement, and data hygiene best practices Participate in strategic discussions related to campaign goals, prospects, portfolios, and pipeline movement by providing analyses, reports, strategies, and other decision-making input Establish and maintain standards for capacity ratings, prospect qualification, and research documentation Evaluate current processes on an ongoing basis and recommend updates to prospect development policies and procedures Prospect Research & Identification Plan and execute strategies to identify major and principal gift prospects using effective research techniques and electronic methodologies, including wealth screening tools Conduct complex and sensitive research assignments personally, including those supporting University leadership and the Board of Trustees Direct the biographical and financial profiling program, ensuring the team produces accurate, well-sourced reports, briefings, and bios for strategy development, events, and meetings Stay informed about national and local news, along with WPI research programs, events, and activities, to use in donor strategy development Principal & Major Gift Strategy Support Serve as a trusted partner and consultant to principal giving officers on engagement activities that advance the cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship cycle of WPI's principal gift donors and prospects Collect and synthesize detailed information on prospective donors to support solicitation and cultivation strategies, and attend meetings that support pipeline movement of assigned prospects Research, collect, and analyze data about assigned donors to identify themes and inform strategies for donor engagement, including events and communications Assist with customized stewardship plans for principal gifts, special donor projects, and division events that help move prospects, including Alumni Weekend, Homecoming, and donor recognition events Team Leadership & Supervision Manage, coach, and mentor the Assistant Director of Prospect Management, including assigning and monitoring work, providing support and development opportunities, and conducting an annual performance evaluation. This includes providing training in research methodologies, resource utilization, and prospect development best practices Foster a collaborative, ethical, and service-oriented team culture aligned with Advancement Operations priorities Professional Expertise & Continuous Improvement Ensure the prospect development program adheres to industry ethics and data privacy standards, including the APRA Statement of Ethics Evaluate research tools, screening platforms, and data sources, and recommend investments that improve team productivity and insight quality Participate in relevant professional associations and training, such as APRA, AFP, and CASE, to stay abreast of industry trends and best practices Performs all other duties and responsibilities as assigned or directed by the supervisor. Qualifications: Minimum of a 4-year bachelor's degree; graduate degree preferred 6-8 years of progressively responsible experience in prospect research, prospect management, or prospect development, preferably in higher education or a complex nonprofit environment Salary Grade 9: $82,600 – $98,000 per year (depending on experience) Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range.  Compensation at WPI FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Professor-of-Practice---Mechanical-and-Materials-Engineering_R0003539": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice | Mechanical and Materials Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Professor of Practice | Mechanical and Materials Engineering LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Mechanical & Materials Engineering DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department at Worcester Polytechnic Institute (WPI) seeks applicants for a full-time teaching faculty position in the area of design as professor of practice. The successful candidate will possess a strong background in engineering design including product development, prototyping and fabrication, and/or design theory and methodology. A commitment to innovative, evidence based teaching is highly desired. The candidate will be expected to contribute to WPI’s project based curriculum by developing and teaching design focused courses at all undergraduate levels, mentoring student project teams, and integrating hands on, experiential learning into the classroom. The ability to collaborate across disciplines and engage students in authentic, open ended problem solving is essential. Candidates should show evidence of effective teaching, related industry experience, or design-focused scholarship. Candidate is required to have a PhD or equivalent degree in mechanical engineering or another relevant discipline or commensurate engineering design experience. JOB DESCRIPTION The Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department at WPI (https://www.wpi.edu/academics/departments/mechanical-materials-engineering) has 26 dual-mission faculty, 8 full-time teaching faculty, and 14 research faculty.  MME offers undergraduate degrees in mechanical engineering to over 1100 students. The department offers graduate degrees in mechanical engineering, materials science and engineering, and manufacturing engineering to about 200 graduate students. The department’s annual externally sponsored research expenditures have exceeded $19.7M. WPI’s reputation as a rigorous and innovative university rests on the shoulders of its faculty. A highly selective, private technological university and one of the nation’s first, WPI believes that when great minds work together, great advances follow. At WPI the boundaries to multidisciplinary collaboration are low—faculty members, students, and other partners work together on the real-world projects and purposeful research that are hallmarks of the WPI experience. Located one hour west of Boston, the university’s campus is in Worcester, Massachusetts, a thriving 21st century college city recognized as a growing hub of scientific and technological innovation. Applications should include curriculum vitae, statements of teaching and research interests, and a list of five professional references. This search will remain open until the position is filled. Questions can be addressed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Professor Sarah Wodin-Schwartz, swodinschwartz@wpi.edu . Salary: $100,000 - $110,000 per year.  Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Director-of-Growth-Marketing_R0003530": {
      "title": "Director of Growth Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Director of Growth Marketing LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Marketing Communications DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Director of Growth Marketing is a member of WPI's in-house team of experts in marketing strategy, messaging, creative, social media, multimedia, and production management. Under the direction of the AVP of Marketing Communications and in collaboration with campus partners, this team leads WPI's integrated brand strategy and the campaigns that support it. With a heavy focus on student enrollment, the Director of Growth Marketing leads strategy and execution of demand generation initiatives that drive awareness, inquiries, and student pipeline growth across undergraduate and graduate studies and pre-collegiate programs. JOB DESCRIPTION Growth Strategy Lead the university's enrollment growth marketing strategy across the full student acquisition funnel, driving awareness, audience acquisition, inquiries, engagement, and pipeline growth through integrated multichannel campaigns, digital nurture programs, and performance optimization across paid, owned, experiential, and CRM-enabled channels. Develop and lead pre-college engagement and retention strategies that cultivate long-term enrollment pipelines, progressing students from WPI middle school and high school programs toward undergraduate inquiry, application, and enrollment. Develop audience segmentation and targeting approaches for prospective students, families, counselors, educators, and other key enrollment influencers, including guidance counselors, superintendents, STEM coordinators, and STEM-focused student organizations. Drive innovation through experimentation, testing, and evaluation of emerging channels, technologies, and audience engagement strategies to improve enrollment marketing performance. Campaigns, Channels & Execution Lead integrated omnichannel enrollment marketing campaigns. Lead planning, execution, optimization, and performance management of enrollment marketing campaigns in partnership with Creative and Digital Operations teams. Lead strategy for enrollment marketing platforms and third-party lead generation ecosystems (e.g., Niche, CollegeVine, U.S. News & World Report), maximizing visibility, engagement, and ROI. Drive continuous improvement of enrollment marketing assets and campaign experiences in partnership with Creative and Digital Operations teams. Work with partners in Admissions to design and optimize CRM-enabled nurture programs and omnichannel student journeys that improve engagement, conversion, and enrollment outcomes. Experiential & Partnership Marketing Lead recruitment-focused experiential marketing initiatives, including conferences, competitions, trade shows, robotics events, and other strategic activations. Manage external marketing partnerships and sponsorships that support prospective student engagement and enrollment growth. Leadership & Cross-Functional Collaboration Lead a team of two marketing professionals, cultivating talent, collaboration, high performance, and a data-driven culture focused on growth and measurable outcomes. Lead cross-functional planning and execution across Admissions, Marketing Communications, Creative, Digital Operations, university stakeholders, agencies, and vendors to deliver integrated enrollment marketing initiatives and measurable business outcomes. Partner with Undergraduate and Graduate Admissions leadership to align enrollment marketing strategies, recruitment priorities, and institutional enrollment goals. Represent the Marketing team in leadership settings and in interactions with stakeholders within the campus community. Provide direction, prioritization, and performance oversight across enrollment marketing campaigns, initiatives, and investments. In partnership with the Creative Director and aligned with the university brand, ensure consistent application of positioning and messaging across recruitment marketing initiatives. Data, Analytics & Performance Use analytics, attribution, and performance insights to optimize marketing investment and campaign effectiveness. Monitor and report regularly on funnel performance, inquiry growth, campaign ROI, and pipeline contribution. Establish testing frameworks and performance benchmarks across creative, audience targeting, messaging, and conversion strategies. Use AI-enabled tools and predictive insights to improve targeting, personalization, operational efficiency, and enrollment marketing outcomes. Performs all other duties and responsibilities as assigned or directed by the supervisor. Qualifications: Bachelor's degree required. A minimum of eight years of progressive experience in growth marketing, enrollment marketing, demand generation, or related marketing disciplines, including at least three years of supervisory experience. Demonstrated success leading enrollment and growth marketing initiatives that drive measurable awareness, inquiry generation, lead acquisition, engagement, and enrollment pipeline growth. Proven ability to develop and execute data-informed marketing strategies across paid, owned, experiential, CRM-enabled, and marketing automation channels. Experience with CRM and enrollment marketing platforms, including Salesforce, Slate, lead generation ecosystems, marketing automation technologies, audience segmentation, nurture campaigns, and prospective student journey development. Strong analytical, strategic thinking, and problem-solving skills, with experience using analytics, attribution, AI-enabled tools, and performance insights to optimize marketing effectiveness and operational efficiency. Demonstrated ability to influence and lead cross-functional teams and initiatives within complex organizations. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, presentation, and stakeholder management skills. Strong project management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, budgets, agencies, sponsorships, external partners, and marketing investments. Proven experience in higher education. Agency, consumer, or direct-to-consumer marketing experience preferred. Salary Grade 10: $100,000 – $124,000 per year (depending on experience) Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range.  Compensation at WPI FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/AV-Technology-Specialist-I_R0003536": {
      "title": "AV Technology Specialist I",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE AV Technology Specialist I LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Academic Technology Center - ATC DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY Coordinate Audio/Visual (AV) equipment reservations for academic use by WPI students, faculty, and staff. Assist with setup, strike, and operation of AV presentation, recording and streaming equipment at various locations on campus to support university initiatives. Manage inventory of laptop computers for temporary loan, event use, and off campus project sites. JOB DESCRIPTION Responsibilities: Provide assistance with set-up and operation of AV equipment in various campus locations for academic and administrative events.  Provide support for virtual events as needed.   Coordinate the laptop imaging process and maintenance of laptops available for loan. Ensure student support staff understand and follow the reimaging protocol.   Create AV equipment reservations based on requests received and coordinate loans with members of the WPI community.  Assist in managing large pool of AV equipment and reservation system.  Conduct annual equipment inventory.   Coordinate the reservation and distribution of laptops for off-campus project sites and summer camp programs.   Assist with front-office operations and provide phone, e-mail, in-person, and on-site support to students, faculty and staff on supported AV systems and equipment.   Provide phone, email, in person and on-site support to students, faculty and staff on supported AV systems and equipment. Assist with the resolution of technology issues experienced by users of campus AV technology.   Capture, edit and catalogue video footage into final product for distribution to appropriate platforms.   Assist with the operations of in-house poster production services as needed.   Train users and student support staff on AV systems and equipment.   Other duties as assigned. Requirements: Associates degree and 2 years or more experience in Communications, Audio/Video Technology and Video Production. Knowledge of AV equipment and hands-on experience in AV set-ups involving laptops, projectors, display resolutions, audio recording, sound mixing, wired and wireless microphones Ability to successfully troubleshoot computer hardware, software, operating system, and peripheral issues A strong willingness to learn the processes of computer imaging Experience using Microsoft Office, including Word, PowerPoint, and Excel Candidate must be customer service driven, have strong written and verbal communication skills as well as excellent presentation and interpersonal skills Candidate must be able to adapt quickly to situations as they arise and have the ability to work independently and as part of a team Ability to lift and transport objects weighing up to 50lbs Candidate must be able to work regular evenings and weekends as assigned The hourly rate for this position is up to $25/hour, depending on experience, for a full time schedule of 40 hours per week. This is equal to $52,000/year annualized. FLSA STATUS United States of America (Non-Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Assistant-Professor_R0003517": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Professor LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Mechanical & Materials Engineering DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department at Worcester Polytechnic Institute (WPI) seeks applicants for a tenure-track faculty position in the area of Applied Artificial Intelligence (AI) for Mechatronics and Controls available at the assistant professor level. JOB DESCRIPTION The successful candidate will possess a strong background in Mechatronics and Controls, demonstrate proficiency in applying AI techniques to these application areas, and strengthen the connection with the Robotics Engineering Department.  Expertise in intelligent sensing and perception, cyber-physical systems, data-driven modeling and control, and AI/deep learning is essential. Applications may include autonomous systems and mobility, intelligent infrastructure, human–robot interaction, smart health, advanced manufacturing and Industry 4.0/5.0, mechatronics for sustainability, and other areas complementary to the department’s existing strengths. A proven ability to integrate multidisciplinary methodologies to solve complex challenges is highly desirable.  The candidate will be expected to develop an active externally funded research program and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in mechanical engineering. Candidate is required to have a PhD or equivalent degree in mechanical engineering, robotics engineering, or another relevant discipline.   This position may be appointed to 25% or a more suitable fraction in the Robotics Engineering Department, as agreed by the successful candidate and the two departments. This position is expected to be filled at the Assistant Professor level. For experienced candidates, rank will be commensurate with experience. The Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department at WPI (https://www.wpi.edu/academics/departments/mechanical-materials-engineering) has 27 dual-mission faculty, 9 full-time teaching faculty, and 12 research faculty.  MME offers undergraduate degrees in mechanical engineering to over 1100 students. The department offers graduate degrees in mechanical engineering, materials science and engineering, and manufacturing engineering to about 200 graduate students. The department’s annual externally sponsored research expenditures have exceeded $ 16M . WPI Robotics Engineering Department ( www.wpi.edu/+RBE ) is the first-of-its-kind department in the nation with a vision to be an exemplary multidisciplinary center of education, research, and innovation in robotics. It is built on an ABET-accredited Robotics Engineering program. RBE counts ~800 undergraduate and graduate students and offers robotics engineering BS, MS, and Ph.D. degrees. In 2016 the Robotics Engineering program was awarded the inaugural ABET Innovation Award for its truly interdisciplinary, project-based curriculum. The department has 23 faculty members and 20+ affiliated faculty members. Our faculty has research support from NSF, NIH, AFRL, Army, ONR, NASA, DARPA, and industry funding. We expect the new faculty member to contribute to the exceptionally close-knit, collaborative, and collegial atmosphere we currently enjoy WPI’s reputation as a rigorous and innovative university rests on the shoulders of its faculty. A highly selective, private technological university and one of the nation’s first, WPI believes that when great minds work together, great advances follow. At WPI the boundaries to multidisciplinary collaboration are low - faculty members, students, and other partners work together on the real-world projects and purposeful research that are hallmarks of the WPI experience. Located one hour west of Boston, the university’s campus is in Worcester, Massachusetts, a thriving 21st century college city recognized as a growing hub of scientific and technological innovation. Applications should include curriculum vitae, statements of teaching and research interests, and a list of five professional references submitted . This search will remain open until the position is filled. Questions can be addressed to the Chair of the Search Committee, Professor Zhu Mao, zmao2@wpi.edu .   Compensation: $105,000 – $118,000 per year. Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Post-Doctoral-Fellow_R0003506": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Post-Doctoral Fellow LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Fire Protection Engineering - NFR JM DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY Applications are being sought for a postdoctoral fellow in the research area of Fire Research with a focus on Wildland-Urban Interface (WUI) fires under the leadership of Prof. James L Urban in the department of Fire Protection Engineering and as part of the Wildfire Interdisciplinary Research Center at WPI (wildfirecenter.com). The position will involve experimental campaigns related to WUI fire exposure, compartment fires, and assisting/contributing to small- and large-scale experiments. The position is for one-year with the possibility of renewal depending on funding. JOB DESCRIPTION Required skills and qualifications: PhD in Mechanical engineering, Fire Protection Engineering, or other related STEM field   Ideal major background will be in the thermal fluids area (fire, fluid mechanics, combustion, or heat transfer)   Strong foundation in thermal fluids     Desired/Optional qualifications: Experience using fire testing equipment :  thermocouples , heat flux gauges, thin-skin calorimeters, pitot-tubes , etc.   Experience with gas sampling and measurements from fire tests   Experience with intermediate to large-scale fire testing   Prior research experience performing physical modelling is a plus   Familiarity with imaging analysis and/or computer vision is a plus.     Applicants will need to provide a letter of interest (1-2pg), a complete CV, at least two exemplar publications, and at least three academic / research references. Applications and associated information will be accepted until the position is filled. Compensation: Salary: $65,000 per year.  Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Dean-of-the-Business-School_R0003503": {
      "title": "Dean of the Business School",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Dean of the Business School LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Provost Office DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY Worcester Polytechnic Institute invites applications and nominations for the position of Dean of the Business School. This is an exceptional opportunity for a visionary leader to advance business education and research at a premier technological university known for its distinctive project-based learning model, where students tackle real-world challenges through hands-on projects that connect academic disciplines to societal needs and professional practice. The Dean will join WPI following the university’s recent achievement of Carnegie R1 research university status and recognition by U.S. News & World Report as No. 18 nationally for best return on investment. This leader will shape the future of WPI’s Business School while contributing to WPI’s continued rise in international prominence. The Business School at WPI is an accredited member of AACSB International, with its industrial engineering program accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET. It offers seven STEM-designated undergraduate programs reflecting emerging technologies and industry needs, including two newly launched degrees in marketing analytics and business analytics & applied AI. At the graduate level, WPI provides MBAs, STEM-designated master’s programs, doctoral programs, and certificates that integrate business fundamentals with analytics, technology, and leadership through hands-on, experiential learning. These offerings emphasize real-world application and allow students and working professionals to build targeted, high-demand skills. The Dean will report directly to Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs and Provost Andrew Sears and serve as a key member of the provost’s leadership team, with a significant opportunity to shape WPI’s academic strategy. Notably, the successful candidate will help guide a time of transformative growth for the school, leading a group of highly motivated, distinguished, and collaborative faculty to significantly expand student enrollment, strengthen interdisciplinary collaboration, forge a robust network of industry relationships, and nurture continued research excellence. The successful candidate will have imagination, resourcefulness, integrity, humility, and the ability to bridge both technical expertise and business acumen. The ideal leader will demonstrate strategic vision, excel at building partnerships across disciplines, and be able to attract top faculty and students while showcasing the school’s unique strengths in bridging technical expertise with humanistic understanding. For full application instructions and the executive search profile, please see the link below. JOB DESCRIPTION The Dean of the Business School provides visionary, strategic, and operational leadership to advance the school’s distinctive role. Academic Leadership Continue the growth trajectory of enrollment. Oversee curriculum development, academic program review, and the accreditation process. Recruit, evaluate, and support faculty in teaching, research, outreach, and professional development. Promote scholarly excellence by leveraging interdisciplinary collaboration within and beyond WPI. Foster a culture of student professionalism, innovation, and success. Provide leadership and oversight for faculty development, resource allocation, and program quality. Champion recruitment, retention, advancement, and well-being to foster a strong, inclusive academic community. Strengthen and expand the school’s research enterprise. Administrative Management Provide strategic and operational oversight of the school, including substantial budgetary responsibility, resource planning, and external representation. Develop and manage the budget, resources, and staffing for the Business School. The Dean will manage a budget of over $7M and provide leadership for the Dean’s Office, comprising four direct reports: Department Head Assistant Dean, Business Programs Assistant to the Dean Operations Manager Lead strategic planning initiatives aligned with institutional goals. Ensure compliance with university policies and relevant external regulations. Ensure decision-making processes reflect fairness, transparency, and ethical stewardship of resources. Student Success & Engagement Support student recruitment, retention, advising, and graduation initiatives. Foster supportive learning environments and co-curricular programming. Address student concerns and uphold academic integrity standards while modeling the professionalism expected of a polytechnic business school. Advance interdisciplinary teaching and scholarship that prepares graduates to address complex global challenges, particularly at the intersection of business, technology, analytics, and societal impact. Champion academic program innovation by working collaboratively with faculty to develop new and responsive programs. Advance the school’s role in WPI’s distinctive project-based learning model. External Relations & Advancement Build and sustain strategic partnerships with industry leaders, international institutions, alumni, and community organizations to enhance research opportunities, enrich student experiences, and elevate the school’s national and global profile. Lead fundraising efforts and secure external grants and sponsorships. Represent the school in university-wide committees and public forums. University-Wide Leadership Serve as an engaged member of the Provost’s Council and the President’s leadership team, contributing to university-wide initiatives while advocating for the school’s mission and strategic priorities. Minimum Qualifications A doctoral degree from an accredited institution in a relevant field, with a record of scholarship and academic leadership appropriate for appointment as a tenured professor at Worcester Polytechnic Institute. A minimum of five years of leadership and administrative experience, including experience in higher education. Proven experience in strategic planning, change management, team building, and budget management, including oversight of complex financial and human resources. Effective leadership and team building across various constituent groups, with the ability to inspire and motivate faculty, staff, and students toward shared goals. Demonstrated success in teaching, research, and service, or equivalent experience in a complex organization. An understanding of and commitment to the evolving nature of a new R1 university. A track record of successful donor stewardship and fundraising. The ability to attract and retain talented faculty, staff, students, donors, and partners. Demonstrated financial acumen and experience managing large budgets and resource allocation. Demonstrated commitment to the highest standards of integrity, ethical conduct, and professional responsibility in all leadership, academic, and administrative activities. Strategic thinking and long-term planning capabilities. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with diverse internal and external communities, and a professional presence appropriate for senior institutional leadership. A willingness to engage with all members of the WPI community, including maintaining a strong presence on campus for school and university-wide programs and events. An innovation-oriented mindset, with the ability to take thoughtful, calculated risks, coupled with an unwavering commitment to the highest standards of personal and professional integrity. Data-informed decision-making and problem-solving skills. Demonstrated engagement with the business community, providing practical insight into contemporary market dynamics, organizational challenges, and workforce needs. Ability to navigate complex organizational structures and drive institutional change. Ability to build partnerships across academic, industry, and community sectors. A record of promoting ethical decision-making and professional conduct within complex academic or organizational environments. For full application instructions and to view the executive search profile, please click here . Compensation: $275,000– $350,000 per year. Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Assistant-Professor---Biology---Biotechnology_R0003488": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor | Biology & Biotechnology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-09\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Professor | Biology & Biotechnology LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Biology & Biotechnology DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Department of Biology and Biotechnology at Worcester Polytechnic Institute invites applications for a full-time tenure track position. The appointment will be at any rank, with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027. JOB DESCRIPTION We seek an outstanding biologist who will enhance and complement the Department’s strengths in cell and molecular biology, microbiology, genomics, bioinformatics, and neuroscience. We are particularly interested in candidates who integrate computational, quantitative, and/or AI-driven approaches with experimentally grounded biological research programs. Competitive applicants will leverage cutting-edge methods in machine learning, systems biology, genomics, imaging, modeling, and/or bioinformatics to address fundamental questions in biology with relevance to biomedical, biotechnological, or environmental applications. Importantly, applicants must demonstrate a strong commitment to experimentally driven research, including a substantive wet-laboratory component within their research program. We seek candidates whose work bridges computation and experimentation. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Biology or a related field (e.g., Computational Biology, Systems Biology, Bioinformatics, Molecular and Cellular Biology, Synthetic Biology, Genetics, or related disciplines), possess substantial postdoctoral experience, and demonstrate a strong record of impactful research. In addition, we expect a commitment to teaching and mentoring of undergraduate and graduate students. This will be demonstrated by strong endorsements from referees, any teaching experience and accomplishments highlighted as part of the application, a statement of teaching philosophy, and sample course materials and teaching evaluations if available. The successful candidate will be expected to pursue vigorous, innovative, and independent internationally recognized research and to establish an outstanding, competitive, and externally funded research program. For more information about the Department of Biology & Biotechnology please visit https://www.wpi.edu/academics/departments/biology-biotechnology and associated research facilities please visit https://www.wpi.edu/research/core-research-facilities/life-sciences-bioengineering-center . Our department has strong links to and shared facilities with the University of Massachusetts Chan Medical School ( https://www.umassmed.edu/ ) in Worcester as well as other institutions in the greater Boston Area. WPI is an outstanding scientific environment with a highly interactive community of researchers recognized globally and nationally for  Interdisciplinary, project-based education that continues to serve as a national model for experiential learning and innovation in STEM education, including recognition with the NAE Bernard M. Gordon Prize A faculty culture that values excellence in both teaching and scholarship within a newly designated R1 research university experiencing rapid growth in research and innovation Progressive promotion and tenure pathways that recognize multiple forms of scholarship and provide meaningful avenues for advancement across teaching, research, and institutional impact A highly collaborative academic environment consistently recognized for faculty satisfaction with interdisciplinary work, mentoring, and collegiality, including top rankings among peer institutions in the COACHE Faculty Job Satisfaction Survey Worcester is a vibrant and cosmopolitan city, home to the WooSox and an  family-friendly place in which to work and live. To Apply: Applicants must submit a cover letter, a current curriculum vitae (including a link to a Google Scholar profile or similar), a research statement outlining current and future research interests (3 pages), and a statement of teaching philosophy and dossier as appropriate (1-2 pages). Applicants must provide the name and contact information of three references. Review of applications will begin on September 11, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Compensation: Academic Year Salary: $90,000 - $100,000 per year.  Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity.  WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Assistant-Professor-of-Information-Systems_R0003453": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Information Systems",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Professor of Information Systems LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME The Business School DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY Do you want to have a greater impact inside and outside the classroom? Worcester Polytechnic Institute (WPI), a premier university located in New England, might be the place for you! WPI's Business School (the Business School) seeks motivated applicants for the position of Assistant Professor of Information Systems (dual mission tenure-track) to build on the university's strengths in the information technology space. We seek motivated applicants with research focused on data analytics, business analytics, databases, machine learning (ML) and artificial intelligence (AI) applications in organizations. Successful candidates must be prepared to conduct high-impact research, publish in high-quality outlets and commit to high-quality teaching. JOB DESCRIPTION Qualifications: Successful candidates will embrace the opportunity to be part of established and new educational and research programs in the growing area of information systems and technology and business analytics. They will distinguish themselves by their interest in collaborating with colleagues from the business school and other departments with technology, engineering, and analytics expertise. A Ph.D. in Information Systems or equivalent is required. Preference will be given to candidates with an ability to engage in high-quality scholarship and high-quality teaching, and have demonstrated interests in analytics, databases, ML/AI applications in organizations and platforms. Candidates should demonstrate ability and willingness to teach at the graduate and undergraduate level. If you are interested in joining our faculty and team of motivated and caring colleagues, you should include: A cover letter A Curriculum Vitae including three references Teaching evaluations Timing: The position will start in August 2027.  We expect to interview at AMCIS 2026 in Reno, Nevada. Review of applications to start on a rolling basis as they come in until the position is filled.   For questions or clarifications, please contact Professor Bengisu Tulu, Search Committee Chair, at bengisu@wpi.edu About WPI:  WPI is a selective private university with a global footprint. It is a place where business and engineering/science collaborate and multidisciplinary teaching and research are encouraged, students excel, embrace challenges, and are independent learners. At WPI, project-based education pervades in the classroom and in a network of more than 40 project centers across the world, innovation is encouraged, a strong sense of a community and the desire to conduct impactful teaching and scholarship prevail. Ranked highly by US News & World Report among national comprehensive universities, WPI enrolls over 4,000 undergraduates and over 2,000 graduate students and enjoys close working relationships with many corporations, due in part to its project-enriched curriculum that engages students and faculty in real-world problem solving. About the Business School: The Business School is not your average business school. Embedded in WPI’s distinctive project‑based learning model and long‑standing strength at the intersection of business, technology, and innovation, The Business School prepares students to lead in data‑rich, technology‑driven environments by integrating rigorous business foundations with analytics, computing, and experiential education. Through real‑world problem solving, interdisciplinary collaboration, and strong industry engagement, The Business School plays a central role in advancing WPI’s mission to address complex global challenges through applied learning and research. The Business School at WPI is a mid‑sized academic unit within a leading STEM university, characterized by close faculty-student engagement and a culture of collaboration. The faculty includes tenure‑track, teaching, and professional practice members whose expertise spans core business disciplines and interdisciplinary areas such as analytics, artificial intelligence, information systems, operations, and entrepreneurship. Faculty are actively engaged in applied scholarship, interdisciplinary scholarship, industry collaboration, and project‑based pedagogy aligned with WPI’s mission. The Business School offers seven STEM designated undergraduate majors (including Business Analytics & Applied AI and Information Systems and Technologies), seven master’s degrees (including STEM designated Information Technology and Business Analytics programs), a Ph.D. degree (with a concentration in Information Technology), and an Executive PhD degree.  The Business School offers faculty members an innovative and collegial educational and research environment, outstanding students, and outstanding support for research and teaching. About the region: With over 200 universities in a 100-mile radius, Worcester Polytechnic Institute is located in the greater Boston area which is known for its dynamic academic environment, thriving economy, rich culture, and quality of life. Compensation: Salary range: $130,000 - $140,000 per year. Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity. WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Assistant-Professor-of-Work-and-Organizations-Organizational-Behavior_R0003447": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Work and Organizations/Organizational Behavior",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Professor of Work and Organizations/Organizational Behavior LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME The Business School DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY Do you want to have a greater impact inside and outside the classroom? Worcester Polytechnic Institute (WPI), a premier university located in New England, might be the place for you! WPI's Business School (the Business School) seeks motivated applicants for the tenure-track position of Assistant Professor in Work and Organizations/Organizational Behavior to build on the university's strengths in the future of work, organizing, and leadership in the digital age. Successful candidates must be prepared to conduct high-impact research, publish in high-quality outlets and commit to high-quality teaching. Candidates with interests in ethnographic and qualitative work are especially encouraged to apply. JOB DESCRIPTION A Ph.D. in management, organization studies, or other related field is required. Preference will be given to candidates with an ability to engage in high-quality scholarship and high-quality teaching, and have demonstrated interests in creativity, innovation, or leadership; how digital tools and technologies (including artificial intelligence (AI)) are transforming workplace dynamics, organizations, careers, and industries; social impact, sustainability and ethics in the age of AI; or leading and managing cross-cultural, cross-disciplinary teams . Candidates should demonstrate ability and willingness to teach at the graduate and undergraduate level. If you are interested in joining our faculty and team of motivated and caring colleagues, you should include: ·       A cover letter ·       A Curriculum Vitae including three references ·       Teaching evaluations Timing: The position will start in August 2027.  We expect to interview at AOM 2026 in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania. Review of applications to start on a rolling basis as they come in until the position is filled.  For questions or clarifications, please contact Elizabeth Long Lingo, Search Committee Chair, at ellingo@wpi.edu . About the Business School: The WPI Business School is not your average business school. Embedded in WPI’s distinctive project‑based learning model, and with long‑standing strengths at the intersection of business, technology, and innovation, The Business School prepares students to lead in data‑rich, technology‑driven environments by integrating rigorous business foundations with analytics, computing, and experiential education. Through real‑world problem solving, interdisciplinary collaboration, and strong industry engagement, The Business School plays a central role in advancing WPI’s mission to address complex global challenges through applied learning and research. The Business School at WPI is a mid‑sized academic unit within a leading STEM university, characterized by close faculty-student engagement and a culture of collaboration. The faculty includes tenure‑track, teaching, and professional practice members whose expertise spans core business disciplines and interdisciplinary areas such as analytics, artificial intelligence, information systems, industrial engineering and operations, and entrepreneurship. Faculty are actively engaged in applied scholarship, interdisciplinary scholarship, industry collaboration, and project‑based pedagogy aligned with WPI’s mission. The Business School offers seven STEM designated undergraduate majors (including Integrated Management Engineering), seven master’s degrees, a Ph.D. degree, and an Executive PhD degree.  The Business School offers faculty members an innovative and collegial educational and research environment, outstanding students, and outstanding support for research and teaching. About WPI:  WPI is a selective private university with a global footprint. It is a place where business and engineering/science collaborate and multidisciplinary teaching and research are encouraged. Our students excel, embrace challenges, and are independent learners. At WPI, project-based education pervades in the classroom and in a network of more than 60 project centers across the world. Innovation is encouraged and a strong sense of a community and the desire to conduct impactful teaching and scholarship prevail. Ranked highly by US News & World Report among national comprehensive universities, WPI enrolls over 4,000 undergraduates and over 2,000 graduate students and enjoys close working relationships with many corporations, due in part to its project-enriched curriculum that immerses students and faculty in real-world problem solving. About the region: With over 200 universities in a 100-mile radius, Worcester Polytechnic Institute is located in the greater Boston area which is known for its dynamic academic environment, thriving economy, rich culture, and quality of life. Compensation: Salary range: $135,000 - $145,000 per year. Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity. WPI’s benefits package includes a robust retirement match, wellness perks, tuition assistance and more! FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Assistant-Swim---Diving-Coach_R0003462": {
      "title": "Assistant Swim & Diving Coach",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Swim & Diving Coach LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Physical Education, Recreation & Athletics - PERA DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY Responsible for assisting the Head Men's and Women's Swimming & Diving Coach as they compete competitively in NCAA Division III athletics while providing an educational environment that enhances the development of the whole student-athlete. Assist the Aquatics Director in all areas of the WPI aquatics facility. Additional responsibilities include teaching courses in physical education as well as departmental administrative responsibilities. JOB DESCRIPTION • Assist the head coach in providing leadership and direction for the Swimming & Diving programs (men’s and women’s). • Create a culture of compliance with NCAA rules and regulations, as well as NEWMAC and WPI university policies and procedures. • Assist in developing team and individual strategies to create an environment of success through effective teaching of technical and fundamental skills in swimming and diving. • Assist in recruiting prospective student-athletes committed to academic and athletic excellence. • Establish ways to ensure success for all team members academically, athletically, and socially. • Assist in maintaining a strong connection with the Swimming & Diving alumni group through communication and relationship development. • Assist with managing the program’s operating and fundraising budgets. • Teach physical education courses. • Perform all other duties and responsibilities as assigned or directed by the supervisor. Requirements • Bachelor’s degree • Certified Pool Operator • 1–3 years of collegiate coaching experience Salary Grade 4: $44,200– $46,189 per year (depending on experience) Salary is based on related experience, expertise, and internal equity; generally, new hires can expect pay between the minimum and midpoint of the range.  Compensation at WPI FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
