    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Summer-Program-Counselor_R0003409-1": {
      "title": "Summer Program Counselor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJOB TITLE Summer Program Counselor LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Mass Academy - JM DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Junior Academy at Mass Academy is a two-week summer program for rising 7th, 8th and 9th grade students from many backgrounds. This day program is designed to provide academic enrichment and support through meaningful learning opportunities so that students will be more confident, curious, and engaged in their learning and realize that science, technology, engineering, and mathematics are not only accessible to them, but they are also rewarding and can open doors for their future. Participating students will receive literacy and math support, engage in hands-on STEM projects, and visit the WPI campus to tour labs and meet researchers. JOB DESCRIPTION Assist teachers during academic classes Provide academic support to individuals and groups of students as needed Foster a positive, educational, and fun community; emphasize mutual respect and inclusiveness Work with other members of the team to plan, organize, and facilitate activities Assist with student drop off and/or pick up Ensure all students check in and check out every day Monitor students throughout the day to ensure student participants adhere to all rules and remain safe; report any concerns to the supervisors as they arise Actively participate in Junior Academy team meetings Work collaboratively with other Junior Academy staff, including teachers Effectively communicate with parents, students, and staff Participate in other aspects of the Junior Academy program (eg. morning meeting and team building activities) Other duties as assigned REQUIREMENTS Qualified candidates will have a growth mindset and believe all students are capable of learning at a high level when given the proper support High school diploma or currently enrolled in high school required Positive attitude, responsible work ethic, and ability to collaborate effectively with a team required. Experience working with children preferred. Strong communication skills required Ability to work on your feet for long periods of time being very active (4-5 hours). May work events that are outdoor and exposure to heat, rain, and inclement weather. An offer is conditional pending a criminal background check. Participate in mandatory training for all staff. Compensation depends on experience but is up to $18/hour. FLSA STATUS United States of America (Non-Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Post-Doctoral-Fellow_R0003347": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-01-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJOB TITLE Post-Doctoral Fellow LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Computer Science - NFR JM DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY One opening is available now for a postdoctoral researcher who will apply machine learning to predict clinical pain related outcomes, participate in an ongoing clinical trial, and assist with app development. The project is sponsored by a National Institutes of Health grant aimed at using machine learning to identify biopsychosocial predictors of the response to a mindfulness intervention for chronic low back pain. The postdoc researcher will be mentored closely while being granted their own freedom of pursuing new research ideas, providing that the progress on the sponsored project is satisfactory. The training of the postdoc will benefit from sophisticated methods development on multidisciplinary research topics, extensive interaction with academic and clinical researchers, and exposure to clinical trial processes and execution. In addition, the postdoc will be able to network with both academic and clinical researchers. JOB DESCRIPTION Responsibilities: The specific job responsibilities include research activities and writing reports and publications. The postdoc is expected to lead research activities, including multimodal data integration and pre-processing , development and validation of predictive machine learning models, communication of the machine learning results to a multidisciplinary team of computational and clinical experts, collaboration on the interpretation of the results in the context of clinical medicine, and preparation of manuscripts for publication. They should be interested in health related research, clinical trials, and app development. Requirements: The requirements for the candidates include: A PhD in Computer Science or in a related computational field. Substantial training in and knowledge of machine learning techniques and strong programming skills. Effective communication in English, both orally and in writing, and ability to interact with multidisciplinary teams. The ideal candidate would have demonstrated interest in and experience applying machine learning to clinical medicine or healthcare. Interest in clinical trials and app development. The existing funding is for one year with a high likelihood of continuing after the first year depending on performance. To apply please include: Cover Letter CV Contact information of 3 referees Position is open until filled. Compensation: $65,000 -$75,000.  This position is supported through external funding. FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Assistant-Coach--Part-time_R0003298": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Part-time",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-11-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJOB TITLE Assistant Coach, Part-time LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Physical Education, Recreation & Athletics - PERA - JM DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY When a vacancy occurs, WPI Athletics will seek part-time assistant coaches for various varsity sport teams. Interested candidates must complete the appropriate applicant information online. The department will directly contact those applicants who are under strong consideration. Please note that candidate applications will remain on file until June 30 each year. JOB DESCRIPTION The primary duty is to assist the head coach in providing leadership and direction for all aspects of the varsity sport program. This includes fostering a culture of compliance with NCAA rules and regulations, as well as WPI university policies and procedures. Responsibilities also include maintaining positive public relations for the program, the department, and WPI, while serving as a role model for student-athletes both in and out of competition. Additionally, the role involves assisting in the preparation of student-athletes for competition and supporting an educational environment that promotes the development of the whole student-athlete. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required Collegiate coaching experience preferred CPR/First Aid/AED certification preferred Valid driver’s license required Compensation : $500 – $7,000 per season This posting covers coaching positions across WPI's entire Club Sports program, resulting in a broad compensation range. Pay is determined by the specific responsibilities of the sport and the coach’s role with the team. This is an excellent opportunity to mentor WPI student-athletes while staying connected to the sport you love. FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
    },
    "https://wpi.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Worcester/Adjunct-Faculty----Philosophy-of-Gender--Race--and-Class_R0003229": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty -  Philosophy of Gender, Race, and Class",
      "description": "Start date: 2025-10-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJOB TITLE Adjunct Faculty - Philosophy of Gender, Race, and Class LOCATION Worcester DEPARTMENT NAME Humanities & Arts - JM DIVISION NAME Worcester Polytechnic Institute - WPI JOB DESCRIPTION SUMMARY The Humanities and Arts Department at Worcester Polytechnic Institute is seeking a part-time adjunct Philosophy faculty member to teach a section of “Philosophy 2716: Gender, Race, and Class” from October 20 to December 12, 2025 on Monday and Thursday afternoons.  The course consists of an examination of categories used to mark social identities of marked difference, such as gender, race, class, sexuality, ability, species, etc. Candidates should have PhD (or ABD) in Philosophy, Women Studies, Gender Studies, Critical Race Theory, or allied fields. JOB DESCRIPTION WPI Philosophy and Religion faculty teach introductory courses, intermediate thematic surveys, and advanced topic seminars. WPI’s PY-RE program has particular strengths in social justice and environmental philosophy; underrepresented philosophical and religious traditions including feminism, critical race theory, and non-Western worldviews; and studies of science, technology, and ethics. We are looking for outstanding scholars, but successful candidates must also demonstrate teaching excellence and versatility as well as an ability to jump into an existing curriculum with creative and critical pedagogical approaches.   Submitting an application for  this part-time posting will place you in an applicant pool to fill Philosophy and Religion adjunct faculty opportunities by the course on an as-needed basis. Specific topics and start dates will vary over the academic year.       Qualified applicants from this applicant pool will be contacted as opportunities arise. Your application will remain in the pool until the posting closes. If you wish to be considered for positions beyond that date, then you must reapply.   Applicants should submit the following: --cover letter that addresses relevant expertise and experience --current c.v. that includes the names and contact information for three references --evidence of teaching experience (syllabi, teaching portfolio, etc.) Compensation: $6,000 per course FLSA STATUS United States of America (Exempt) WPI is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, age, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or disability. It seeks individuals from all backgrounds and experiences who will contribute to a culture of creativity, collaboration, inclusion, problem solving, innovation, high performance, and change making. It is committed to maintaining a campus environment free of harassment and discrimination."
